    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nA new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is now still created, and the response reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`).\n\n## How it fits the existing architecture\n\nI followed the established OfficeFloor create pipeline and the existing \"counter\" step convention (`CountNamesakes`, `CountHousehold`):\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`, a single-responsibility function that reads the built `Owner` (`@Val`), scans `OwnerRepository.findAll()` for a same-lastName (case-insensitive, matching the namesake convention) + same-postcode + different-telephone owner, and stamps `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` in place. It runs *after* `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (so hard duplicates are already rejected) and *before* `SaveOwner` (so the new owner isn't matched against itself), under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours. Picks the earliest match id for determinism.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted `flagPossibleDuplicate` between `countNamesakes` and `save` in `owners.POST.yml`.\n\n3. **Model** \u2014 two fields + getters/setters on `Owner` (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`).\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four DB schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, postgres, mysql).\n\n5. **API contract** \u2014 added the two `readOnly` fields to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; MapStruct maps them onto the DTO automatically by name (no explicit mapping needed), which the passing GET-based assertion confirms.\n\nNo existing class grew a new responsibility \u2014 the detection lives in its own step, and postcode/telephone/name comparisons reuse the already-normalized values the pipeline produces upstream.",
